"program_narrative": "Program ERRHNDL is an online (CICS) centralized error handler that receives an error description in its commarea (copybook ERRHND layout). It copies the commarea into working storage, stamps the error with the current date/time and generates a trace ID when none was supplied. It then logs the error by inserting a row into the DB2 table ERRLOG (program, paragraph, SQLCODE, CICS response, severity, message, trace ID); if the insert fails the message is replaced by 'Error logging failed' and the error is escalated to fatal. Next it reformats the error message as 'Error in <program> - <message> (<trace id>)' and decides the recovery action from the severity: fatal errors get action Abend, warnings and informational errors get action Continue, anything else gets action Return. The updated error area is copied back to the commarea and control returns to CICS. The four steps are invoked with PERFORM ... THRU ranges (flagged as unstructured), and two statements need SME review: MOVE FUNCTION RANDOM into an alphanumeric trace ID and a STRING whose receiving field ERR-MESSAGE is also one of its sources.",
